_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.2.stable.official [46dc27791]\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev4.official [bd2ca13c6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev4 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8088) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 61.64 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen HDR 2D is enabled, using the save image functions (`save_jpg`, `save_png`, and `save_webp`) of `Texture2D` produce a dark image:\n\n| HDR 2D disabled | HDR 2D enabled\n| -- | --\n| <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52cc13e1-fd5b-43cb-a62b-0b02d258cfe2\" />| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7cca6d8f-b7ab-4793-ab8a-b6ee745e6f00)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable HDR 2D in the project settings\n2. Create a new 3D scene\n3. Add a camera and world environment\n4. Save the image `Texture2D.save_jpg` or equivalent:\n\n``` GDScript\nvar image := get_tree().root.get_viewport().get_texture().get_image()\nimage.save_jpg(\"jpg.jpg\")\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[screenshot-saver-hdr-2d.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23613252/screenshot-saver-hdr-2d.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenw